## Why This Is Asked

This probes security-first real-time design under multi-tenancy, focusing on trusted execution, key management, and safe rollback under partitions.

## Key Concepts

- TEEs and attestation for secure compute
- Deterministic tenant routing and per-tenant model/versioning
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant KEKs and rotation
- In-enclave streaming processing and leakage minimization
- Canary rollout, drift testing, and backfill under partitions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: fetch KEK, decrypt features in enclave, and score
async function scoreTenantEvent(event, tenantId){
  const kek = await kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  const plain = decryptInHost(event.encryptedFeatures, kek);
  const score = enclave.computeScore(tenantId, plain, getModelVersion(tenantId));
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and mitigate side-channel risks in this setup?
- How would you validate model version rollbacks across regions during a canary release?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cross-region, multi-vendor aggregation pipeline with tamper-evident auditing and model_versioning. It checks API design, data modeling, robust aggregation, and rollout/rollback in production.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region data ingestion and weighting
- Poisoning resistance and drift detection
- Versioning, canary rollouts, rollback
- Auditability and security controls

## Code Example
```javascript
function trimmedMean(arr, trim=0.1){
  const sorted = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const k = Math.floor(n * trim);
  const sliced = sorted.slice(k, n - k);
  return sliced.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) / sliced.length;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor region skew and detect collusion? 
- How would you validate a rollback doesn’t impact older clients or data streams?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world need for a multi-tenant policy engine to enforce per-tenant constraints without downtime.

## Key Concepts
- Policy-as-code and versioning
- Per-tenant gating and feature flags
- Zero-downtime updates, revocation, and rollback
- Observability and auditing for policy changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy check
function checkPolicy(tenant, request) {
  const p = policyStore.get(tenant);
  if (!p) return false;
  if (request.model_version !== p.allowedModel) return false;
  if (!p.allowedRegions.includes(request.region)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test policy revocation safety under traffic spikes?
- How would you handle cross-region policy replication and consistency?
